WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.147
Gucci Dionysus 
bag. Is it worth it?

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.755
I'm Tanner. I've been
deconstructing

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.924
and inspecting designer
luxury leather bags

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.861
to help people understand
if it's worth it or not,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.362
and I'm going to 
walk you through

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:33.666
how I deconstruct the $1,100
Gucci Dionysus mini bag.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.104
The most misused 
term in the industry,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.073
it's "genuine leather."

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.610
It may mean really low
qualities of leather,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.447
and some people use it 
in very misleading ways.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.816
I try to put my estimate

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.985
on the leather and 
craftsmanship costs

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.854
so people can make
that deduction.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.589
Like, how much of this price

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.858
is now status coming
from the brand?

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.861
And make your mind
by yourself, right?

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.764
I look at three things.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.032
First is leather.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.401
Like, what type of
leather selection

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.703
was employed in this design?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.940
How good of a 
leather is required

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.242
for this kind of finish 
they employed here?

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.612
Two is the craftsmanship,

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.781
the sophistication
of the design.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.651
And finally, the third one is

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:28.121
overall performance value

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.156
compared to that price point.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.791
If you're looking
for just leather,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.859
you don't care 
about the status,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.127
it might be too much for you.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.863
And if you are OK,
you want to buy

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.431
the status that comes
with the brand,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.766
then it's totally 
worth it for you.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.936
So that's my intention
of helping people

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.404
with this information.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:47.040
This buckle is attached
to it very strongly

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.708
through these 
metal connections,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.810
and it is really hard 
for me to take it off,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.513
so I am cutting the buckle
off from the leather

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.181
to take it out of my way

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.250
so we can start 
inspecting the leather.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:02.388
Gucci bag has about
two, three layers

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.357
of supporting 
materials inside.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:07.360
The leather is backened
by this fabric,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.663
which will prevent the 
stretching of the leather over time,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.166
so it's going to 
make sure the form

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:17.003
stays intact in years to come.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.838
There are some 
thicker supports

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.674
almost resembling 
cardboard kind of materials.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.210
Sometimes leather
dust is employed

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.180
in those support 
materials as well

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.383
to increase the structure
rigidity of the bag.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.287
This Dionysus bag was very
rigid and structured bag.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.557
It looked, felt, and
stayed very solid

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.526
in its given form,

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.728
and it was very
well executed.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.363
Super-good craftsmanship,

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.931
very good design,
and all that.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.568
Internal pieces was 
carefully planned, selected,

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:52.138
and the stitching lines,

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:56.309
even the count of the 
stitches, quality seems really good.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:00.180
I think the shop 
making this bag,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.684
definitely a top-notch
artisan shop.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.819
Now I'm applying
some acetone,

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:10.256
because it's a very common
household dissolver,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:14.127
and I'm using a sharp knife,

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:18.031
or a little leather blade,
to remove the finish.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.066
It's technically 
like scraping off

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.102
a little bit of a cream 
from top of the leather,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.371
and there is no certain depth.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.007
I go until I see 
the leather grain.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.443
By leather grain, I'm 
talking about the pores

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:33.880
of the hair cells, actually.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.816
You will start seeing the 
hair cells beyond the finish

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:41.387
once those plasticky, 
gooey substance is gone.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:45.024
And that gooey substance,
it's just liquidized plastic.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.096
The finish on it,

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.165
that pattern-embossed
finish,

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.700
is a thick, heavy finish.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.002
Underneath, when
I open the bags,

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.304
I know this is good 
leather after touching it,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.973
seeing the backside
of it, and all that.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.107
This is subjective.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:04.143
The leathers I love has
this minimal finish

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.446
where I see the natural
grain of leather,

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:09.816
because leather is a 
non-standard natural material,

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.683
just like, you know,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:13.019
everybody's skin looks
slightly different.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.355
Truly minimally finished
artisan leathers

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.789
make unique pieces.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.892
No two leather 
craft will look alike.

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.394
That's what I 
appreciate in leather,

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:24.163
but I know this is really
almost impossible

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.867
for big brands to go 
with due to their size.

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.869
They need some form
of standardization.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.773
Now I'm going to 
cut really thin strips

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.907
so I can burn it

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.744
and understand from the
burning characteristics

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:40.713
what kind of tanning was
involved in this leather.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.684
Leather can be tanned
different ways.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.252
They all burn 
slightly differently,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:49.055
and they leave different
residues, ashes.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.823
Chrome-tanned leather
burns really slow.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.059
You have to force 
it to keep burning.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:56.696
And then the ashes
will usually show

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.132
some form of green residue,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:02.435
which is the color of the
chrome tanning agent.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:07.173
90%, in my estimate, of 
leathers are chrome-tanned,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.109
because it's convenient, 
easy, quick, and very durable,

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:13.579
and everybody uses it,
but it's a heavy metal,

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:17.317
and it's more polluting in
the tanning technique.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:23.656
Metal-free leather is a fairly
new tanning technique,

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.458
I would say only 
becoming more popular

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.493
in the couple decades.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:31.931
Gucci bag has a 
metal-free claim.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:35.234
And grain, sometimes
they call it grain

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:38.137
or pebbled calfskin leather,

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.774
and this is the little 
pebbles they refer to

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.543
when they're 
talking about that,

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:46.412
which is a 
standardization finish.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.981
So the leather they used here

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.384
is showing me no 
signs of chrome,

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:55.822
which is confirming their 
claim of metal-free tanning,

00:05:55.822 --> 00:06:00.193
and that's as much as I
can tell from this test.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.495
It doesn't tell too 
much of the details

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.564
when you're talking about
metal-free tanning,

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:07.033
but at least we don't 
see signs of chrome.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:11.938
In my opinion, this bag 
can be made about $115

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:14.707
in leather and labor,
material cost.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.409
It was definitely well made.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.178
It's beautiful leather
employed here.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:23.116
The quality of craftsmanship
and accessories is exceptional.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:25.318
Of course, it's a big
brand. It's Gucci.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.153
There is a premium, 
definitely, you're paying

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.389
in the price of $1,100,

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.957
because eventually,

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:33.326
regardless how good 
of a leather you use,

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.628
price doesn't go 
above a certain point

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:36.863
because of the leather.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:40.533
Then, when you start 
seeing astronomical prices,

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.602
you know that it's not 
about the leather anymore,

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.971
it's about the status that
comes with the price.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.473
That's the whole point
of my question of,

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.008
is it worth it or not?

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.810
Leather is not cheap,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.813
but it's never 
astronomically expensive.

